{
  "//": [
    "Typecheck config for the capture GUI. HAND-WRITTEN AND COMMITTED.",
    "",
    "`ags types -u` writes its OWN `tsconfig.json` into this directory and",
    "OVERWRITES it on every run, so that file is gitignored and is NOT what the",
    "typecheck reads. This file deliberately uses a non-colliding name so the",
    "settings below survive regeneration. `make capture-typecheck` passes it",
    "explicitly with `-p tsconfig.capture.json`.",
    "",
    "Why this gate exists at all: `ags bundle` TRANSPILES WITHOUT TYPE CHECKING.",
    "Verified — `const bad: number = \"string\"` bundles with exit 0. So without",
    "this, a wrong signature reaches production silently. See design.md §1.1.",
    "",
    "Everything under @girs/, env.d.ts and node_modules/ is GENERATED by",
    "`ags types` (168 files, ~49 MB of machine-specific GTK/Astal declarations)",
    "and is gitignored — see .gitignore. Regenerate with `make capture-types`."
  ],
  "compilerOptions": {
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    // AGS ships its own JSX runtime; without this, JSX resolves to React types.
    "jsxImportSource": "ags/gtk4",

    "module": "ES2022",
    "moduleResolution": "Bundler",
    "target": "ES2020",
    "strict": true,

    // REQUIRED. The generated @girs declarations contain ~47 duplicate
    // GTK3/GTK4 identifier clashes. They are not our code and not our bug;
    // without this the gate is red on files we do not own.
    // (design.md §1.2)
    "skipLibCheck": true,

    // REQUIRED. gnim (pulled in via the node_modules symlink) calls
    // String.replaceAll, which is ES2021+. Without DOM/ES2022 lib, gnim fails
    // to compile. (design.md §1.2)
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM"],

    // REQUIRED — PINS THE AMBIENT-TYPE SURFACE TO EMPTY, ON PURPOSE.
    //
    // This app runs under GJS, not Node. It has no `process`, no `Buffer`,
    // no `require`. Declaring no "types" makes TypeScript auto-include EVERY
    // @types/* package reachable by the default typeRoots walk from THIS
    // directory upwards — so the app's ambient surface silently depended on
    // where a directory happened to live.
    //
    // Today @types/node sits at tests/node_modules/ — installed there on demand
    // by `make capture-test` — which that walk does not descend into, so the app
    // is clean by TWO independent guards rather than by luck. Move @types/node
    // anywhere the walk reaches (capture-tool/node_modules/, or the repo root)
    // and 66 of its files join the app program — verified with `tsc --listFiles`
    // at this revision. That puts Node's globals in scope for GJS code that must
    // not use them, so the install location below is a real constraint and not
    // a preference.
    //
    // `[]` makes that arrangement stop mattering: the surface is empty whether
    // or not @types/node is reachable, and `make capture-test` keeps the install
    // out of the walk anyway. Two guards, deliberately. The tests are a SEPARATE project
    // (tests/tsconfig.tests.json) which asks for `"types": ["node"]` by name,
    // so they still get exactly what they need.
    //
    // NOTE: this pins the surface but was NOT, by itself, causing ~96 app
    // errors — see design.md §2 ("The phantom") for what actually happens.
    // Verified: 0 errors in src/gui-tools/capture-tool either way. The leak
    // was real; the catastrophic blast radius was not.
    "types": []
  },
  "include": [
    // App sources. Globs, not a file list, so the A3–A8 layer directories are
    // covered the moment they appear without editing this config.
    "*.ts",
    "*.tsx",
    "ui/**/*.ts",
    "ui/**/*.tsx",
    "lib/**/*.ts",
    "domain/**/*.ts",
    "ports/**/*.ts",
    "adapters/**/*.ts",

    // REQUIRED. @girs/index.d.ts `import`s every generated GIR module in
    // turn, so naming it here is what pulls the whole transitive closure in.
    // Without it every `gi://GLib?version=2.0` style import is unresolved and
    // JSX handler parameters degrade to implicit `any` — ~101 spurious
    // errors. (design.md §1.2)
    "@girs/index.d.ts",

    // Generated ambient declarations for `*.css`, `*.scss`, `*.blp`, `inline:*`.
    "env.d.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "bin", "tests"]
}
